# Keep the Marine extension byte-identical on every platform.
#
# tauri.conf.json ships `../marine-extension` into the app verbatim, so whatever
# git writes into a checkout is exactly what reaches the user's browser.
donut/marine-extension/** text=auto eol=lf

# ...and never translate the Scholay generated assets at all.
#
# sw.js (`marineLoadGeneratedSkillAssets`) SHA-256s each of these files and
# compares it against `assetHashes` in manifest.json. That check runs inside the
# PUT branch of `marineContextFetch`, *before* the fetch — so a mismatch does not
# corrupt a diff, it throws, the rime-context PUT is never sent, the comment
# target never publishes, and the 「生成」 button sits at 「准备中…」 until it fails
# with 「目标准备超时」. The message blames the input box and the local service;
# both are wrong, which makes this near-impossible to diagnose from the symptom.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true and CI checks out with a bare
# actions/checkout@v4 on windows-latest, so without this rule these files arrive
# CRLF on the Windows runner and every hash misses — breaking comment generation
# on Windows builds only, while macOS builds work. Marking them binary is what
# guarantees the bytes the hashes were computed over are the bytes that ship.
donut/marine-extension/skills/scholay/generated/*.json -text
